  data: {
    LLM: 'The object is to avoid scoring penalty points. Each heart scores its pip value (2–10 at face value, jack 11, queen 12, king 13, ace 14; queen of spades 25). The game is played to a higher target (e.g. 500); the player with the lowest score when someone reaches or exceeds the target wins.\n\nPlay follows standard Hearts. The holder of the 2 of clubs leads it to the first trick. Players must follow the suit led if possible; the highest card of the suit led wins the trick. Hearts may not be led until a heart has been played to a previous trick (hearts broken), unless a player holds only hearts. Shooting the moon (taking all penalty cards) reverses the score for that hand. Deal and passing cycle are as in standard Hearts.',
    Player: 'The object is to avoid scoring penalty points. Each heart scores its pip value (2–10 at face value, jack 11, queen 12, king 13, ace 14; queen of spades 25). The game is played to a higher target (e.g. 500); the player with the lowest score when someone reaches or exceeds the target wins.\n\nPlay follows standard Hearts. The holder of the 2 of clubs leads it to the first trick. Players must follow the suit led if possible; the highest card of the suit led wins the trick. Hearts may not be led until a heart has been played to a previous trick (hearts broken), unless a player holds only hearts. Shooting the moon (taking all penalty cards) reverses the score for that hand. Deal and passing cycle are as in standard Hearts.',
